  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "This plant arose from a witches'-broom growing on the ever-popular 'Sango kaku' and discovered by the late Ilo Sorenson from the Blue Mountains near Sydney, Australia. It has retained all the characteristics of its famous parent—the beautiful coral-red shoots and the five-lobed palmatum-type leaf shape, size, and coloring. The notable difference is that 'Fjellheim' is much bushier and shorter. Although in young plants, vigorous shoots may extend to 1. 5 m, growth slows down with age. Hence, 'Fjellheim' forms a much more compact bush than"
  },
